---
import { withBase } from "../lib/urls";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Topbar from "../components/Topbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/sections/Footer.astro";
import About from "../components/sections/About.astro";
import ScrollFade from "../components/ScrollFade.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import "../styles/manifesto.css";
import excerpts from "../content/manifesto-excerpts.json";
const firstStanza = [
  "I saw a satellite and an aeroplane and all the boats against the current",
  "Come gathering ’round the ocean to watch the old rocket fly",
  "At thirty-two hundred kelvin, even God ain’t no deterrent",
  "For the cosmonaut, the vessel man, who looked up at scary skies",
];
const chorus = [
  "UP TOWARD THE APOLUNE IS WHERE I LIVE OR WHERE I DIE",
  "BORNE TOWARD THE FAR POINT AND THE GOLDEST OF GOLDEN LIGHT",
  "OH, LEST I LOSE MY MAGIC OR MY SWEET OLD LULLABYES",
  "YEAH, ONWARD AND UPWARD, MAN, WHERE I MAKE IT WORTH THE FIGHT",
];
const lastStanza = [
  "said a man who was promised the moon, a most human inheritance",
  "In silence shrunk down to a thumb-held pound coin",
  "And in the highest of all stillnesses, he bore the ring of an ancient marriage, since",
  "every wounded work is what the love of it will anoint",
  "and join the whole of you and the hurt of you as you touch the sweetest star",
  "and dwell before the earthrise as evidence of the oldest frame, set, and mark",
  "catching fading dreams, burning witness to the dark",
  "and the stories from the far, far point. alas, we can’t help but chase the spark.",
];
---
<Base title="Our Manifesto | Up Toward the Apolune" description="The striving, more than the product, is what counts. Apolune’s manifesto for handmade, literary, imperfect work, centred on a poem by Ansel Tan.">
  <Topbar />
  <main class="manifesto">
    <section class="manifesto-hero" aria-labelledby="manifesto-title">
      <div class="manifesto-wrap">
        <div class="manifesto-running-head"><p>APOLUNE / OUR MANIFESTO</p><span>VANCOUVER · EST. 2026</span></div>
        <div class="manifesto-hero-grid">
          <div class="manifesto-hero-copy">
            <p class="manifesto-kicker">FOR THE WONDER OF CREATING.</p>
            <h1 id="manifesto-title">Up toward<br />the <em>Apolune.</em></h1>
            <p class="manifesto-hero-intro">To make narrative work with the care of art, not just the efficiency of a product, and to chase great storytelling for nothing but the wonder of creating.</p>
            <a class="manifesto-read" href="#the-poem">A POEM. A POINT OF DEPARTURE. <Icon name="arrow-right" size={20} /></a>
          </div>
          <figure class="manifesto-rocket"><img src={withBase("/assets/manifesto/rocket.webp")} alt="A spacecraft and rocket on a floodlit launch pad, surrounded by smoke" width="650" height="597" fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption>Ambition, human striving, and the silence just beyond.</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
        <div class="manifesto-hero-foot"><span>STORIES FROM THE FAR POINT.</span><a href="#the-far-point">KEEP READING ↓</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <About showManifestoLink={false} />

    <section id="the-far-point" class="manifesto-paper manifesto-section" aria-labelledby="far-point-title">
      <div class="manifesto-wrap manifesto-editorial-grid">
        <div class="manifesto-margin-note"><span>01 / THE FAR POINT</span><svg viewBox="0 0 260 155" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="112" cy="77" rx="96" ry="33" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" transform="rotate(-16 112 77)"/><circle cx="90" cy="77" r="26" fill="currentColor"/><circle cx="207" cy="51" r="5" fill="#bb2932"/><path d="m210 40 15-18" stroke="#bb2932" fill="none"/><text x="173" y="17" fill="currentColor" font-size="10">THE APOLUNE</text></svg></div>
        <ScrollFade><div class="manifesto-prose">
          <h2 id="far-point-title">The striving,<br /><em>more than the product,</em><br />is what counts.</h2>
          <p>Our name is borrowed from astronomy.</p>
          <figure class="manifesto-definition">
            <blockquote>“the point in an elliptical orbit around the Moon where a spacecraft or satellite is at its greatest distance from the Moon's center”</blockquote>
            <figcaption><cite>Definition adapted from <a href="https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/apolune" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Merriam-Webster: apolune</a>.</cite></figcaption>
          </figure>
          <p>We imagine the APOLUNE to be a place of the cutting-edge. It is the culmination of ambition and human striving — but it is also a place of a sombre, deeply human inheritance. One imagines the Apolune both wondrous and slightly lonely, as fleeting as it is high, a testament to the turn of a life of creation.</p>
          <p>We believe that to create is to create with the full knowledge that we inhabit the in-between, to accept it anyway, and to have faith that we will continue shooting for the far point, however imperfect.</p>
        </div></ScrollFade>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="the-poem" class="manifesto-poem-section manifesto-section" aria-labelledby="poem-title">
      <div class="manifesto-wrap">
        <header class="manifesto-poem-heading"><p class="manifesto-kicker">THE POEM AT THE HEART OF IT</p><h2 id="poem-title">UP TOWARD THE APOLUNE</h2><p>By Ansel Tan</p></header>
        <div class="manifesto-poem">
          <p class="manifesto-stanza">{firstStanza.map((line) => <span>{line}</span>)}</p>
          <div class="manifesto-refrain"><p class="manifesto-poem-lead">and said</p><blockquote>{chorus.map((line, i) => <span>{i === 0 ? '‘' : ''}{line}{i === chorus.length - 1 ? '’' : ''}</span>)}</blockquote></div>
          <p class="manifesto-stanza">{lastStanza.map((line) => <span>{line}</span>)}</p>
        </div>
        <p class="manifesto-poem-note">“every wounded work is what the love of it will anoint”</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="manifesto-art-spread manifesto-paper" aria-label="Concept paintings from Apolune’s creative world">
      <figure><img src={withBase("/assets/manifesto/the-journey.webp")} alt="Two people facing each other in a warmly lit train carriage, with mountains beyond the window" width="1600" height="785" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>“said a man who was promised the moon, a most human inheritance”</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src={withBase("/assets/manifesto/the-sky.webp")} alt="A painted figure resting on a green hillside beneath a blue sky and passing aircraft" width="1600" height="1084" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>“and join the whole of you and the hurt of you as you touch the sweetest star”</figcaption></figure>
    </section>

    <section class="manifesto-making manifesto-section" aria-labelledby="making-title">
      <div class="manifesto-wrap manifesto-editorial-grid">
        <p class="manifesto-margin-note">02 / THE WORK OF OUR HANDS</p>
        <ScrollFade><div class="manifesto-prose">
          <h2 id="making-title">Handmade.<br />Literary.<br /><em>Imperfect.</em></h2>
          <p>Apolune is a Vancouver-based production house and creative collective dedicated to telling STORIES FROM THE FAR POINT. We began with a simple goal: to make narrative work with the care of art, not just the efficiency of a product, and to chase great storytelling for nothing but the wonder of creating. Over time, that has grown into a vision that includes our own slate of narrative films, commercials, and music videos.</p>
          <p>We believe in preserving the handmade, literary, poetic, and ultimately imperfect nature of our work.</p>
        </div></ScrollFade>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="manifesto-machine manifesto-section" aria-labelledby="machine-title">
      <div class="manifesto-wrap manifesto-machine-grid">
        <p class="manifesto-margin-note">FROM <em>LAMENT FOR THE MACHINE</em><br />ANSEL TAN</p>
        <h2 id="machine-title" class="manifesto-machine-heading">The creator’s<br /><em>dream.</em></h2>
        <div class="manifesto-machine-copy">
          <blockquote class="manifesto-machine-excerpts"><p>{excerpts.real}</p><p>{excerpts.tools}</p></blockquote>
          <p class="manifesto-emphasis">{excerpts.dream}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="manifesto-risk manifesto-paper manifesto-section" aria-labelledby="risk-title">
      <div class="manifesto-wrap">
        <p class="manifesto-kicker">FROM <em>LAMENT FOR THE MACHINE</em> · ANSEL TAN</p>
        <h2 id="risk-title" class="manifesto-risk-heading">The distance was never<br /><em>made of resolution.</em></h2>
        <blockquote class="manifesto-risk-quote manifesto-risk-excerpt">“{excerpts.risk}”</blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="manifesto-belief manifesto-section" aria-labelledby="belief-title">
      <div class="manifesto-wrap manifesto-belief-grid">
        <figure class="manifesto-bellwood"><img src={withBase("/assets/the-angel-liberty.webp")} alt="A painted angel reaching toward a paper airplane among roses and a red-lit sky" width="1672" height="941" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The spirit of St. Bellwood.</figcaption></figure>
        <ScrollFade><div class="manifesto-prose">
          <p class="manifesto-kicker">03 / A LITTLE FAITH</p>
          <h2 id="belief-title">She tries<br /><em>regardless.</em></h2>
          <p>Our angel is an epigraph of a fictional character called St. Bellwood, from one of our original pieces.</p>
          <p>From a field of plasticine roses, cast in the light of a neon television, Bellwood works tirelessly to build cardboard wings for herself to fly.</p>
          <p>Her belief in her ability exceeds even her capacity to succeed. But she tries regardless.</p>
          <p>So we carry on the way you’d carry a candle across a windy field: one hand cupped around the flame, knowing it might go out, walking anyway. We cast the bell without knowing whether it will ring, and we wait to hear.</p>
          <p class="manifesto-emphasis">That’s what we call FAITH ... that it’s worth the walking.</p>
        </div></ScrollFade>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="manifesto-together" aria-labelledby="together-title">
      <img class="manifesto-coast" src={withBase("/assets/manifesto/the-long-road.webp")} alt="Two figures on a painted coast looking toward a church above the cliffs" width="1600" height="1128" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="manifesto-together-copy manifesto-wrap">
        <p class="manifesto-kicker">04 / NEVER VERY FAR FROM EACH OTHER</p>
        <h2 id="together-title">A borrowed light.<br />A crew of friends<br /><em>who said yes.</em></h2>
        <p>When we’re not working on our in-house productions, we act as an end-to-end production service helping clients and creatives around the world bring their stories to life. We also host community events like the Apolune Film Festival to bring storytellers together in-person, because we know first-hand that the best work rarely gets made alone.</p>
        <p>Every collaboration starts with someone saying “I loved your film. What are you making next?”</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="manifesto-close manifesto-section">
      <div class="manifesto-wrap">
        <p class="manifesto-kicker">ONWARD AND UPWARD, MAN.</p>
        <h2>We can’t help<br /><em>but chase the spark.</em></h2>
        <p>The FAR POINT is where that faith lives: past the budget, past the odds, past anyone’s permission, out where the work is its own reason.</p>
        <div class="manifesto-actions"><a class="landing-link" href="mailto:hello@apolune.net">MAKE SOMETHING WITH US <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a><a class="landing-link" href={withBase("/#hero")} >EXPLORE OUR WORK <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a><a class="landing-link" href={withBase("/film-festival")} >THE FILM FESTIVAL <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a></div>
        <p class="manifesto-sources">Poem and selected excerpts by Ansel Tan. From <em>UP TOWARD THE APOLUNE</em>, <em>Lament for the Machine</em>, and Apolune’s founding vision.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
